<!--
    "Nos engagements" — four claims in a row, icon above two lines of text.
    No cards and no heading: the strip is a reassurance band that sits quietly
    under the hero, so the claims themselves carry it.

    The icons are the client's own artwork, inlined rather than linked as image
    files so they can take their two colours from the block's CSS variables —
    a palette change stays a one-line edit.

    Each export arrived with its own <style> block defining .st0/.st1 in
    slightly different hexes. Inline SVGs share a single CSS scope, so keeping
    them would have let the last icon recolour the other three; the styles are
    stripped and the fills mapped to .s_tecas_ink / .s_tecas_accent instead.
    Their id="Layer_1" is dropped too — four copies of one id is invalid html.
-->
